WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.962
The power structure at
The Morning Show

00:00:03.962 --> 00:00:07.591
is shifting with the new voices
and younger generations.

00:00:07.591 --> 00:00:09.760
We have some fabulous
new cast members.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.470
We have more
incredible storylines,

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:13.222
we have new amazing characters.

00:00:13.555 --> 00:00:15.724
Okay, should we have the
conversation about Bradley

00:00:15.724 --> 00:00:17.851
that I think we're all thinking?
Is she really cutting it?

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:21.688
Greta came in and just swooped
us all off of our feet.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.649
What I want is to
change things here.

00:00:23.649 --> 00:00:26.610
Stella Bak is the youngest and

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:30.322
only female news president in
the history of UBA.

00:00:30.322 --> 00:00:31.657
I want to build things but I

00:00:31.657 --> 00:00:34.201
can't build them if the
ground isn't level.

00:00:34.201 --> 00:00:36.745
She's essentially the new
Cory Ellison, so there's

00:00:36.745 --> 00:00:39.373
no reason why they would get
along and see eye to eye

00:00:39.373 --> 00:00:41.208
and they definitely do
butt heads.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:43.835
Her point of view seems to be
you're lucky to have me

00:00:43.835 --> 00:00:45.587
clear the wax out of your
ears so you

00:00:45.587 --> 00:00:46.630
can hear what I'm telling you.

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:48.882
UBA's New Year's Eve
extravaganza

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.259
tomorrow night live.

00:00:50.259 --> 00:00:52.678
I've spent years putting on a
suit pretending

00:00:52.678 --> 00:00:55.555
to be a fake news anchor
so transitioning

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.641
over to The Morning Show was
just an extension.

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:58.684
And action!

00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:00.936
I was asked to submit my

00:01:00.936 --> 00:01:04.231
audition tape during my
sister's wedding.

00:01:04.231 --> 00:01:07.442
I call mom, I said will you sing
with me really quick?

00:01:07.442 --> 00:01:09.152
We did a little duet together,

00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:10.821
and that was the weirdest
audition tape

00:01:10.821 --> 00:01:12.447
I've ever put together
in my life.

00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:15.784
The top trending topic this
morning is Alex Levy.

00:01:15.784 --> 00:01:18.745
When Ty comes into this world
he's new and fresh

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:21.248
and he's not involved
with the internal games

00:01:21.248 --> 00:01:23.750
and mechanics of trying to get
up the ranks of UBA.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:24.584
Hello.

00:01:24.376 --> 00:01:26.295
Who are you and how
did you get in here?

00:01:26.295 --> 00:01:28.297
Oh that's Ty Fitzgerald he's
actually on the show.

00:01:28.297 --> 00:01:29.756
I know who that is.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.925
I was really nervous to
act opposite Jen.

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.844
I really am so looking forward
to working with you.

00:01:33.844 --> 00:01:38.348
Well I'm really excited to be
worked, uh, with- worked with.

00:01:38.348 --> 00:01:39.224
Yes.

00:01:39.224 --> 00:01:41.351
She was so friendly and so
supportive that

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:43.353
I forgot about
all my anxieties.

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:45.355
Well look who's here.

00:01:45.355 --> 00:01:48.483
Julianna Margulies is an
incredible addition to the show.

00:01:48.483 --> 00:01:49.443
There she is.

00:01:49.443 --> 00:01:50.068
Here I am.

00:01:50.068 --> 00:01:52.112
She's brilliant and so talented.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.447
She was on "ER" and 
I was on "Friends"

00:01:53.447 --> 00:01:56.283
and our stage doors opened
and we'd chat with each other.

00:01:56.283 --> 00:01:58.702
Who would've thought
twenty-five years later

00:01:58.702 --> 00:02:00.454
we'd be, finally on
the same set?

00:02:00.454 --> 00:02:01.371
Alex if you're ready.

00:02:01.371 --> 00:02:04.708
My character, Laura Peterson,
is the network's golden ticket.

00:02:04.708 --> 00:02:06.209
She can pretty much do
anything she wants.

00:02:06.209 --> 00:02:10.756
What was the nature of your
relationship with Mitch Kessler?

00:02:10.756 --> 00:02:13.717
You never see anything like it,
someone coming in so

00:02:13.717 --> 00:02:15.927
well-prepared take
after take, after take.

00:02:15.927 --> 00:02:18.013
It's just quite impressive.

00:02:18.388 --> 00:02:21.391
It was an incredible experience,
coming into this show where

00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:24.644
everybody on this set is a
master of their craft.

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:27.856
Jumping into this vat of
incredibly talented women,

00:02:27.856 --> 00:02:29.399
it was an embarrassment
of riches.

00:02:29.399 --> 00:02:30.984
I'm so excited to come to work

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:33.862
and to get to do it with
these people who I love,

00:02:33.862 --> 00:02:34.905
It's a total dream.

00:02:34.905 --> 00:02:36.365
♪♪

